issue.description:
Refine the recently added theme export surface so it is presented as a focused code-view/copy experience rather than a generic export/download flow.

## Goal

Rename the header action and dialog around the concept of theme code, remove the now-unneeded download flow, and improve the code panel structure and scrolling.

The resulting interaction should feel like:

Code
→ Theme code dialog
→ choose JSON or Tailwind CSS
→ inspect code
→ copy code

## 1. Rename the header action

Change the existing header action label from:

**Export**

to:

**Code**

Update the icon accordingly.

Requirements:

* replace the current export/download icon with an appropriate existing code icon;
* prefer an already-installed Lucide code glyph such as `Code2` or the closest accepted equivalent;
* preserve the action's current position in the header;
* preserve keyboard/focus/accessibility behavior;
* accessible name should match the visible action: **Code**.

Do not retain export/download semantics in the iconography.

## 2. Rename the dialog

Change the dialog title from:

**Export theme**

to:

**Theme code**

## 3. Simplify the supporting copy

Replace the current verbose description with concise copy:

**Copy your theme as JSON or Tailwind CSS.**

Requirements:

* keep the copy directly beneath the dialog title;
* use the existing muted/supporting text treatment;
* do not include the current theme name in the paragraph;
* do not mention downloading.

## 4. Remove Download

Remove the Download action entirely from this dialog.

Requirements:

* no Download button in the footer;
* no file download behavior from this dialog;
* no unused footer space left behind;
* remove obsolete download-specific handlers/state/tests where safe;
* keep JSON and CSS generation intact because both remain available for preview/copy.

The dialog should become copy-oriented rather than file-export-oriented.

## 5. Move Copy into a code toolbar

Move the Copy action out of the dialog footer.

Add a slim toolbar/header directly above the code content.

Toolbar behavior:

* visually attached to the code panel;
* Copy aligned to the right;
* use the existing Copy icon;
* button should contain:
  * Copy icon
  * `Copy` label;
* preserve existing copied-state feedback if present;
* Copy must continue copying the exact currently displayed format output.

The toolbar should read as part of the code surface rather than as a global dialog footer.

Prefer a subtle divider between the toolbar and code viewport.

## 6. Code panel structure

The code panel should conceptually be:

code panel
├─ toolbar
│  └─ Copy
└─ scrollable code viewport

Preserve:

* monospace rendering;
* whitespace/newlines;
* read-only behavior;
* exact preview/output equality;
* JSON / CSS format switching.

Do not add code editing.

## 7. Use the existing shadcn ScrollArea

Replace the current/native-looking code scrollbar treatment with the accepted shadcn ScrollArea component already used elsewhere in the Workbench.

Requirements:

* reuse the existing Workbench ScrollArea implementation/pattern;
* do not introduce a new scrollbar library;
* keep scrolling local to the code viewport;
* keep the dialog itself contained on narrow and wide viewports;
* preserve keyboard scrolling;
* avoid page-level overflow;
* keep code readable at long output lengths.

The scrollbar should visually match other Workbench scroll surfaces.

## 8. Format selector

Preserve the existing format selector:

* JSON
* CSS / Tailwind v4

Changing formats must continue to update the code preview immediately.

Do not redesign the selector as part of this ticket unless a tiny spacing adjustment is necessary to integrate the revised code panel.

## 9. Preserve code generation contracts

Do not change:

* canonical Theme v3 JSON serialization;
* JSON import compatibility;
* current Tailwind v4 CSS renderer;
* light/dark CSS output;
* built-in/custom theme output semantics;
* Theme v3 schema;
* persistence/history;
* Design Command;
* mutation operations;
* public registry.

This is primarily an interaction/presentation refinement.

## 10. Accessibility

Verify:

* Code header action has an appropriate accessible name;
* dialog title is exposed correctly;
* Copy remains keyboard accessible;
* Copy icon is decorative when accompanied by visible label;
* ScrollArea remains keyboard-scrollable;
* Escape and close-button behavior remain unchanged;
* focus trap and logical tab order remain intact;
* format selector remains keyboard operable.

## 11. Verification

Verify at minimum:

* header action now reads **Code**;
* header action uses an appropriate code icon rather than export/download icon;
* clicking Code opens the dialog;
* dialog title is **Theme code**;
* supporting copy reads exactly:
  * `Copy your theme as JSON or Tailwind CSS.`
* Download button and file-download path are absent from the dialog;
* Copy appears in the code toolbar with the Copy icon;
* Copy copies the exact visible JSON output;
* Copy copies the exact visible CSS output;
* changing formats updates preview and Copy target correctly;
* code viewport uses the existing shadcn ScrollArea pattern;
* long JSON/CSS output scrolls cleanly;
* narrow/wide dialog containment remains correct;
* focus, Escape, close, and keyboard scrolling remain correct;
* no regression to JSON/CSS generation or Theme v3 contracts.

## Acceptance

* Header action is renamed from Export to **Code**.
* Header icon is changed to an appropriate code icon.
* Dialog title is **Theme code**.
* Dialog supporting copy is exactly **“Copy your theme as JSON or Tailwind CSS.”**
* Download functionality is removed from the dialog.
* Copy is moved into a toolbar directly above the code viewport.
* Copy includes an appropriate existing Copy icon.
* Code scrolling uses the existing shadcn ScrollArea pattern.
* JSON and CSS preview/copy output remains exact and unchanged semantically.
* No Theme v3, persistence, Design Command, mutation, registry, dependency, network, or public API regression is introduced.
